    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §104-c, Gen Muni L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5667\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend\nthe general municipal law, in relation to authorizing the disposal of\ncomputers through donation to not-for-profit institutions for use by\nsenior citizens or low income individuals\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nThis bill would authorize not-for-profit institutions to receive\ndonated computers from municipalities for use by senior citizens and\nlow income individuals.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nCurrent law authorizes municipalities to donate unused computers to\nschools and libraries and also authorizes not-for-profit institutions\nto receive donated computers from municipalities for use by\nindividuals with disabilities.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThere are many not-for-profit institutions which are currently not\nincluded in law that would benefit from donated computers from\nmunicipalities and this legislation allows for more of these\ninstitutions to receive such computers.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nThis is a new bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately, with provisions.\n\n",
